{"notes": "Realised inflation is accelerating on a 3-month annualized basis, with headline CPI rising to 3.47% annualized and monthly momentum picking back up to +0.27% m/m. The 3-month core print at 1.92% annualized is less concerning but shows a tick from the lows, and core is running above its 12-month low. However, inflation expectations have softened meaningfully on the 21-day horizon (down 0.02pp to 1.86%), sitting 0.14pp below the 2% target and near the bottom of its recent range at 1.66% low. The 63-day and 252-day slopes on breakevens are flatter, with the 63-day at +0.10pp showing only modest recovery.

The labour market remains tight but has cooled. The unemployment rate is at a 12-month low of 4.20%, but has been range-bound recently and the 3-month/6-month changes are -0.20pp, indicating a plateau rather than continued deterioration. The Sahm gap sits at a benign +0.03pp and the rate sits 20bps above the estimated natural rate, suggesting slack is present but not dramatic.

