{"notes": "Realized inflation has collapsed sharply off multi-year highs. Headline CPI fell from 2.60% y/y to 0.20% y/y over the last three months (a 2.4pp drop), with month-on-month readings turning deeply negative; core PCE is also down 0.7pp to 1.00%. This is base-effect driven — the 3m annualized headline read of -5.21% shows the magnitude of the disinflationary momentum. But 10-year breakevens have barely budged. They fell 26bp over 63d and 58bp over 252d, but are near the middle of their 12-month range and sit only 85bp below the 2% target. The recent 21d move is essentially flat (+1bp).

