{"notes": "Inflation has surged dramatically, with headline CPI reaching 4.92% y/y and core PCE at 3.54% y/y — both now 1.5+ pp above target. More telling is the momentum: headline is annualizing at 7.49% over three months and mom prints have held above 0.48% for the outgoing period. Core has accelerated similarly to 6.14% annualized. The labor market remains tight with unemployment at 5.8%, only 1.8 pp above natural rate, having fallen 0.4 pp in three months. Both inflation and labor tightness are moving the same direction — higher and tighter respectively — which normally signals persistent upside to inflation pressure.

