{"notes": "Realised inflation is hot and accelerating; expectations are cracking under the weight of it, but not fast enough or far enough. Headline CPI sits at 6.90% yoy, up 1.75pp in three months, with near-term momentum elevated (0.86% mom, 9.48% annualized 3m). Core PCE at 4.44% yoy, a smaller but still material +0.51pp in three months, sits 2.44pp above target. This is not a base-effect story: the 3m annualized runs are the centrepiece, and labour tightness remains extreme — unemployment at 4.1%, down 2.6pp in twelve months, with a Sahm gap of only 0.33pp, indicating little slack and strong wage-setting power.

