{"notes": "Inflation itself is in steady disinflation mode, but expectations are not. Realised headline CPI has dropped 0.59pp over the past three months on an annualised basis (3.13% now vs 3.72% three months ago), and core PCE has fallen 0.83pp (3.47% vs 4.30%), both tracking well below the 2.73% and 2.31% annualised 3m rates respectively—evidence of further momentum to the downside. The monthly burn is cooling too: the 3-month average of headline MoM stands at 0.22%, with the outgoing print at just 0.02%, almost 21bps below the recent trend. Core remains 147bps above target, but the trajectory is unambiguous.

